    "### 7.4 Observations\n",
    "\n",
    "* Identifiers, quantities, and ratings are stored as integer values (`int64`).\n",
    "* Prices and monetary values are stored as floating-point values (`float64`).\n",
    "* Descriptive attributes are stored as strings (`str`).\n",
    "* Four date-related attributes are currently stored as strings (`str`): `orders.order_date`, `reviews.review_date`, `shipments.shipment_date`, and `shipments.delivery_date`.\n",
    "* These date-related attributes should be converted to a datetime type (`datetime`) to facilitate filtering, sorting, and subsequent temporal analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 8. Numeric Value Validation\n",
    "\n",
    "### 8.1 Objective\n",
    "\n",
    "Analyze the distribution of numeric attributes and identify potential outliers or inconsistencies using statistical measures such as minimum and maximum values, quartiles, median, and interquartile range (IQR).\n",
    "\n",
    "### 8.2 Code"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "37f2b2a2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "numeric_columns_for_outliers = {\n",
    "    \"orders\": [\"total_price\"],\n",
    "    \"order_items\": [\"quantity\", \"price_at_purchase\"],\n",
    "    \"products\": [\"price\"],\n",
    "    \"payments\": [\"amount\"],\n",
    "    \"reviews\": [\"rating\"]\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "outlier_analysis = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for table_name, columns in numeric_columns_for_outliers.items():\n",
    "\n",
    "    df = tables[table_name]\n",
    "\n",
    "    for column in columns:\n",
    "\n",
    "        series = df[column].dropna()\n",
    "\n",
    "        q1 = series.quantile(0.25)\n",
    "        q3 = series.quantile(0.75)\n",
    "        iqr = q3 - q1\n",
    "\n",
    "        lower_limit = q1 - 1.5 * iqr\n",
    "        upper_limit = q3 + 1.5 * iqr\n",
    "\n",
    "        outliers = series[\n",
    "            (series < lower_limit) |\n",
    "            (series > upper_limit)\n",
    "        ]\n",
    "\n",
    "        outlier_analysis.append({\n",
    "            \"table\": table_name,\n",
    "            \"column\": column,\n",
    "            \"q1\": q1,\n",
    "            \"q3\": q3,\n",
    "            \"iqr\": iqr,\n",
    "            \"lower_limit\": lower_limit,\n",
    "            \"upper_limit\": upper_limit,\n",
    "            \"outlier_count\": len(outliers)\n",
    "        })\n",
    "\n",
    "outlier_analysis_df = pd.DataFrame(outlier_analysis)"
   ]
  },
