    "## 13. Conclusions\n",
    "\n",
    "The e-commerce data analysis made it possible to identify several patterns related to customer behavior and product performance.\n",
    "\n",
    "**1. Customer Behavior**\n",
    "\n",
    "Customers with the highest total spending are not necessarily those who place the most orders. The three customers with the highest recorded spending have only two orders each. This shows that the value of individual purchases can have a greater impact on total spending than the number of orders placed.\n",
    "\n",
    "**2. Customer Segmentation**\n",
    "\n",
    "The segmentation based on total spending shows that 42.55% of customers belong to the Low segment, 38.50% to the Medium segment, and 18.95% to the High segment.\n",
    "\n",
    "Overall, 81.05% of customers belong to the Low or Medium segments, while 18.95% belong to the High segment.\n",
    "\n",
    "**3. Product Performance**\n",
    "\n",
    "The product with the highest total revenue was `Water Bottle`, generating $63,822.93 in revenue from 92 units sold.\n",
    "\n",
    "In contrast, `Wireless Mouse` recorded 118 units sold but generated $53,935.18 in revenue. This demonstrates that selling a higher number of units does not necessarily result in higher revenue, as the selling price also influences the final outcome.\n",
    "\n",
    "**4. Product Identification**\n",
    "\n",
    "The analysis also showed that different products can have the same name, such as `Standing Desk`. For this reason, `product_id` should be used as the primary identifier to distinguish products and avoid grouping different records solely by product name.\n",
    "\n",
    "**5. Application of SQL**\n",
    "\n",
    "The project provided an opportunity to apply different SQL techniques to solve data analysis problems, including:\n",
    "\n",
    "* `JOIN` and `LEFT JOIN` to relate tables.\n",
    "* `GROUP BY` to perform aggregations.\n",
    "* `COUNT()` and `SUM()` to calculate metrics.\n",
    "* `COALESCE()` to handle null values.\n",
    "* `CASE WHEN` to create customer segments.\n",
    "* CTEs (`WITH`) to divide complex queries into logical stages.\n",
    "* `RANK()` and `PARTITION BY` to perform rankings within each category.\n",
    "* `ORDER BY` to sort and organize results."
